Date: Fri, 8 Oct 93 2:19:17 PDT
From: szabo@netcom.com (Nick Szabo)
Subject: GUNS, SOC: Burglary and countermeasures

I find the argument of justice, that the "punishment should
fit the crime", to be absurd applied to the case of people
who break into my home.  This isn't punishment or revenge or
justice, it's self defense.  The main outcome I'm concerned about 
not how much they lose, but how little my household loses.
Nor am I concerned about (im)balance between the two.

Furthermore, it can be dangerously wrong to assume the intruder is
unarmed, so hesitating at the injustice of shooting an unarmed
intruder is especially pernicious.  

The main reason to be concerned about shooting intruders, and it's a
quite important one, is the problem of distinguishing freind from foe.
Freinds who think they have the right to enter unannounced, 
unannounced and unescorted guests of housemates, etc.  Where
those are situations are at all probable I basically
eliminate the option of shooting intruders.

