>
>CONFERENCE AND EXHIBITION
>
>   This important conference will showcase a range of ongoing projects,
>studies  and  initiatives  that  reflect  Russia's needs for changes in
>higher   education,   and   the   application   of   new   information,
>telecommunications, and distance education technologies  in the Russian
>educational and training sectors.
>
>   It  will  stimulate  the investigation and discussion of a number of
>practical  approaches  to  introducing  Russians  to the new democratic
>educational  system   and  market-oriented  economy   through  distance
>learning and mass media,  as  well as to providing Russian students and
>adults  with  worldwide telecommunciations access to higher educational
>institutions and training agencies.
>
>   The  conference  will  become  the  vehicle for defining strategies,
>identifying  priorities,  allocating  funds and providing facilities to
>various locally initiated training projects.
>
>   The  goal  of  the  exhibition is to demonstrate modern information,
>communications,  and  multimedia   technologies,   along   with   their
>applications  in  Russian  education  and  training  contexts.  It will
>provide  conference  participants with information on the state-of-the-
>art  in  creating  the learning environments and classrooms of the 21st
>century.
>
>
>TOPICS OF THE CONFERENCE
>
>   The conference will be divided into two principal areas within which
>discussions and meetings will take place.
>
>Distance Education:
>   *       Theory
>   *       Quality and Standards; Recognition and Academic Mobility
>   *       National and International Aspects
>   *       Higher Education; Training and Re-training
>   *       National Innovative Projects
>   *       International Initiatives in Russia
>   *       Priorities and Strategies
>   *       Economics, Management and Marketing of Distance Education
>
>Educational Environment:
>   *       Information Technologies in the Classroom
>   *       Electronic Tutors and Testing Systems
>   *       Multimedia
>   *       Audio- and Video-Conferencing
>   *       Computer Mediated Communications
>   *       Innovative Solutions
>
>
>INVITED SPEAKERS
>
>  Internationally recognized keynote speakers are being invited to make
>presentations on the main topics of the conference.
>
>
>DEMONSTRATIONS
>
>   The  conference  will  serve as well as a site for the showcasing of
>technologies  and  processes.  Projects, equipment, and software can be
>demonstrated,  and  completed  or  ongoing distance learning or working
>projects are particularly welcome.
>
>   The Information Systems  Research  Institute  of  Russia,  which  is
>responsible  for  the  Federal  program  for  the  development  of  new
>information  technologies  in  Russian  higher  education,  will  award
>limited   number   of   grants  to  support  selected  projects.  Other
>organizations and foundations are invited to observe the  presentations
>of ongoing projects and other activities.
>
>   Please  contact  the Conference Secretariat if you wish to present a
>demonstration, and request the special form to submit a description  of
>your project or product.
>
>
>EXHIBITION
>
>   The  exhibition  will  be  open  for  the  display  and operation of
>equipment,  systems,  software  and other products or processes used in
>distance learning. Organizations,  corporations,  and  institutions are
>invited to present their educational  products  and  to  carry on other
>activities supportive of distance learning and international education.
>
>   Special  guest  tours  of  decision-makers  and experts from Russian
>Ministries,  governmental  agencies,  state  and  private companies and
>institutions will  be visiting  the  exhibition,  and  invitations  are
>being  sent  to  many  other  important people from the  user/purchaser
>community  in  Russia.  Also, the winners of a national competition for
>creative software  will demonstrate their products to potential western
>partners.
>
>   Exhibitors  are  asked  to  contact  the  Conference Secretariat for
>further information.
>
>
>SUBMISSION OF PAPERS
>
>   The  official  languages  for  presentations are Russian and English.
>Translation  facilities  will  be  provided  on  request.  But  all  the
>presented papers must be in English.
>
>   Prospective  presenters  must  submit  the  following  to the Program
>Committee by January 1, 1993, by e-mail in plain ASCII form:
>  (i)   completed Presenter Proposal Form;
>  (ii)  a one-page abstract suitable for the conference program booklet;
>  (iii) a paper written  in  English,  noe exceeding 5000 words.
>
>   Please indicate which  topic  you feel your paper should be presented
>under.
>
>   Acceptance of a paper  implies  a  commitment  on  the  part  of  the
>author(s) to present it  at  the  conference.  Accepted  papers  will be
>published in the proceedings.
>
>   Final  decisions  on  acceptance  of  papers  for the 1994 conference
>proceedings  will  be  made  by the Programme Committee of international
>experts by February 1, 1994. All presenters will be notified.
>
>
>KEY DATES
>
>January  1, 1994:   Deadline of submission of abstracts and full papers.
>February 1, 1994:   Notification of acceptance/rejection of papers.
>March    1, 1994:   Preliminary programme will be published.
